  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><msub><mn>10</mn><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>22000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>L</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math> is equal to _____."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "221",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mfenced><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>K</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>10</mn></mmultiscripts></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>22000</mn><mi>L</mi></math></p><p>Now taking L.H.S we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo>.</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>.</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>9</mn></mmultiscripts></math></p><p>Now using the rule that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>&#183;</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mi>n</mi></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mi>n</mi><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi></mrow></mmultiscripts></math></p><p>So using the above formula we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></munderover><msup><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>10</mn></msup><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mfenced><mmultiscripts><mi>C</mi><mn>9</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>18</mn></mmultiscripts></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mn>18</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4862000</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>22000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>22000</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>221</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>22000</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math></p><p>Now on comparing we get,</p><p>Hence&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>221</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
